'''Divine Flare''' is a [[debuff]] from the monster skill of the same name. It is used by the boss [[Dawn, Harbinger of Solaris]] and its map variants [[Jorus, Sky's Edge]] and [[Opid, Helial's Herald]]. The debuff deals [[burning damage]] ([[fire]] [[damage over time]]).

It is also used by another unique monster [[Cato, Scholar of Light]] (and his map variant [[Barthol, the Pure]]), but with different internal id: [[Skill:BlackguardClericBossHolyCannon|BlackguardClericBossHolyCannon]]. When Cato/Barthol changed to second phase as [[Cato, Defiler of Light]] ([[Barthol, the Corruptor]]) he uses {{stl|Heretical Flare}}.

Unlike its storyline variant, [[Suncaller Asha]] ({{il|Park Map}}) also uses Divine Flare.

Note that the vertical fire beam in the [[Solaris and Lunaris]] boss fight, it does not have the Divine Flare status icon despite looking similar.

Divine Flare is in fact coded as a minion.<ref name=DivineFlareDawn/> The "monster" is not targetable and does not have a nameplate. It has a skill that deals the actual damage. For [[Dawn, Harbinger of Solaris|Dawn]] case, it is known as [[Skill:InvisibleIonHolyCannonDawn|InvisibleIonHolyCannonDawn]] internally.<ref name=DivineFlareDawn>[[Monster:Metadata/Monsters/InvisibleFire/InvisibleHolyCannonMoveDaemon]]</ref> While Dawn only acts as the AI that interact with the Divine Flare AI.
==Monsters==
The following [[monster]]s summon Divine Flare skill or use skill that command Divine Flare to move:
{{#cargo_query:
|tables=monsters
|fields=CONCAT("[[", _pageName, "|", name, "]]")=Monster names, skill_ids
|where=(skill_ids HOLDS LIKE "%MoveDaemonIonCannon%" OR skill_ids HOLDS LIKE "%HolyCannon%") AND name NOT IN ("Daemon", "Invisible" , "Shaman of the Feast") 

|limit=100
|order by=name
}}

The following "[[monster]]s" use Divine Flare (or similar) skills:
{{#cargo_query:
|tables=monsters
|fields=CONCAT("[[", _pageName, "|", name, "]]")=Monster names, metadata_id, skill_ids
|where=skill_ids HOLDS LIKE "%InvisibleIonHolyCannon%" 

|limit=100
|order by=name
}}

